{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6wuX1DUMCQNoUoGCwH9Yp","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"STUB Stage-B host — a runnable stand-in for ``gandalf-run.mjs``.\n3\t\n4\tWired in via ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD`` (e.g. ``python tests/stub_gandalf_host.py``)\n5\tso a Gandalf engine test never invokes real ``node`` / the real Skill-Foundry\n6\thost. It reads the RAW draft on stdin (exactly as ``gandalf-run.mjs`` does) and\n7\temits a canned GRADED ``advisor-output.json`` (the 9 required top-level keys per\n8\t``schema/advisor-output.schema.json``) on stdout, exit 0.\n9\t\n10\tHonesty knobs (so the degrade path is testable):\n11\t- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_FAIL=1`` → write an honest stderr reason + exit 1 (the\n12\t  host's malformed/non-conformant non-zero-exit contract).\n13\t- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_BADJSON=1`` → emit non-JSON on stdout (unparseable output).\n14\t- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_DEGRADED=1`` → set ``degraded:true`` on the graded output.\n15\t- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_CROSSMODEL=1`` → set ``cross_model:true``.\n16\t- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_VERDICT`` → override the top-level verdict text.\n17\t\n18\tThe stub honors the real host's stdin contract; it does NOT re-implement the\n19\tseam pass — it returns a deterministic, schema-shaped graded object so the Anchor\n20\tflow (parse → validate → render → store) is exercised end-to-end. NEVER live.\n21\tStdlib only.\n22\t\"\"\"\n23\timport json\n24\timport os\n25\timport sys\n26\t\n27\t\n28\tdef _flag(name):\n29\t    raw = os.environ.get(name)\n30\t    return bool(raw) and raw.strip().lower() not in (\"0\", \"\", \"false\", \"no\")\n31\t\n32\t\n33\tdef main():\n34\t    # Read (and ignore the content of) the raw draft, honoring the stdin contract.\n35\t    try:\n36\t        _ = sys.stdin.read()\n37\t    except Exception:\n38\t        _ = \"\"\n39\t\n40\t    if _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_FAIL\"):\n41\t        sys.stderr.write(\"gandalf-run(stub): conformance failure — no output \"\n42\t                         \"written.\\nforced failure for the degrade test\\n\")\n43\t        return 1\n44\t\n45\t    if _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_BADJSON\"):\n46\t        sys.stdout.write(\"this is not json — host produced garbage\\n\")\n47\t        sys.stdout.flush()\n48\t        return 0\n49\t\n50\t    verdict = (os.environ.get(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_VERDICT\")\n51\t               or \"This is broadly sound, with one durability gap worth watching.\")\n52\t\n53\t    graded = {\n54\t        \"schema_version\": \"1\",\n55\t        \"cross_model\": _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_CROSSMODEL\"),\n56\t        \"degraded\": _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_DEGRADED\"),\n57\t        \"reasoning\": \"The deterministic seam pass stamped the raw draft; \"\n58\t                     \"elevations land SPECULATIVE (no independent challenger ran).\",\n59\t        \"verdict\": verdict,\n60\t        \"findings\": [\n61\t            {\n62\t                \"id\": \"d-1\",\n63\t                \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n64\t                \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n65\t                \"reasoning\": \"The test gate runs green at the documented baseline.\",\n66\t                \"verdict\": \"The build is in a healthy, tested state.\",\n67\t                \"severity\": \"minor\",\n68\t                \"gandalf_core\": {\"protocol\": \"PROTOCOL v2\"},\n69\t            }\n70\t        ],\n71\t        \"nitpicks\": [\n72\t            {\n73\t                \"id\": \"n-1\",\n74\t                \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n75\t                \"reasoning\": \"A few docstrings drift from the current behavior.\",\n76\t                \"verdict\": \"Minor doc drift; low stakes.\",\n77\t            }\n78\t        ],\n79\t        \"elevations\": [\n80\t            {\n81\t                \"id\": \"e-1\",\n82\t                \"tier\": \"SPECULATIVE\",\n83\t                \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n84\t                \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n85\t                \"reasoning\": \"A periodic re-analysis would catch drift earlier \"\n86\t                             \"(no independent refutation ran).\",\n87\t                \"verdict\": \"Consider scheduling a recurring read.\",\n88\t            }\n89\t        ],\n90\t        \"risk_labels\": [\n91\t            {\"leg\": \"diagnose\", \"tier\": \"SPECULATIVE\", \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\"}\n92\t        ],\n93\t    }\n94\t\n95\t    sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(graded, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n96\t    sys.stdout.flush()\n97\t    return 0\n98\t\n99\t\n100\tif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n101\t    sys.exit(main())\n102\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8879e2bf-702b-4c2f-a33b-7fb98e48e304","uuid":"9b04654d-8889-4803-9e1e-12e653a92b6b","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:33:40.701Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\tests\\stub_gandalf_host.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"STUB Stage-B host — a runnable stand-in for ``gandalf-run.mjs``.\n\nWired in via ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD`` (e.g. ``python tests/stub_gandalf_host.py``)\nso a Gandalf engine test never invokes real ``node`` / the real Skill-Foundry\nhost. It reads the RAW draft on stdin (exactly as ``gandalf-run.mjs`` does) and\nemits a canned GRADED ``advisor-output.json`` (the 9 required top-level keys per\n``schema/advisor-output.schema.json``) on stdout, exit 0.\n\nHonesty knobs (so the degrade path is testable):\n- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_FAIL=1`` → write an honest stderr reason + exit 1 (the\n  host's malformed/non-conformant non-zero-exit contract).\n- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_BADJSON=1`` → emit non-JSON on stdout (unparseable output).\n- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_DEGRADED=1`` → set ``degraded:true`` on the graded output.\n- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_CROSSMODEL=1`` → set ``cross_model:true``.\n- ``STUB_GANDALF_HOST_VERDICT`` → override the top-level verdict text.\n\nThe stub honors the real host's stdin contract; it does NOT re-implement the\nseam pass — it returns a deterministic, schema-shaped graded object so the Anchor\nflow (parse → validate → render → store) is exercised end-to-end. NEVER live.\nStdlib only.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\n\n\ndef _flag(name):\n    raw = os.environ.get(name)\n    return bool(raw) and raw.strip().lower() not in (\"0\", \"\", \"false\", \"no\")\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Read (and ignore the content of) the raw draft, honoring the stdin contract.\n    try:\n        _ = sys.stdin.read()\n    except Exception:\n        _ = \"\"\n\n    if _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_FAIL\"):\n        sys.stderr.write(\"gandalf-run(stub): conformance failure — no output \"\n                         \"written.\\nforced failure for the degrade test\\n\")\n        return 1\n\n    if _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_BADJSON\"):\n        sys.stdout.write(\"this is not json — host produced garbage\\n\")\n        sys.stdout.flush()\n        return 0\n\n    verdict = (os.environ.get(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_VERDICT\")\n               or \"This is broadly sound, with one durability gap worth watching.\")\n\n    graded = {\n        \"schema_version\": \"1\",\n        \"cross_model\": _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_CROSSMODEL\"),\n        \"degraded\": _flag(\"STUB_GANDALF_HOST_DEGRADED\"),\n        \"reasoning\": \"The deterministic seam pass stamped the raw draft; \"\n                     \"elevations land SPECULATIVE (no independent challenger ran).\",\n        \"verdict\": verdict,\n        \"findings\": [\n            {\n                \"id\": \"d-1\",\n                \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n                \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n                \"reasoning\": \"The test gate runs green at the documented baseline.\",\n                \"verdict\": \"The build is in a healthy, tested state.\",\n                \"severity\": \"minor\",\n                \"gandalf_core\": {\"protocol\": \"PROTOCOL v2\"},\n            }\n        ],\n        \"nitpicks\": [\n            {\n                \"id\": \"n-1\",\n                \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n                \"reasoning\": \"A few docstrings drift from the current behavior.\",\n                \"verdict\": \"Minor doc drift; low stakes.\",\n            }\n        ],\n        \"elevations\": [\n            {\n                \"id\": \"e-1\",\n                \"tier\": \"SPECULATIVE\",\n                \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n                \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n                \"reasoning\": \"A periodic re-analysis would catch drift earlier \"\n                             \"(no independent refutation ran).\",\n                \"verdict\": \"Consider scheduling a recurring read.\",\n            }\n        ],\n        \"risk_labels\": [\n            {\"leg\": \"diagnose\", \"tier\": \"SPECULATIVE\", \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\"}\n        ],\n    }\n\n    sys.stdout.write(json.dumps(graded, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False) + \"\\n\")\n    sys.stdout.flush()\n    return 0\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n","numLines":102,"startLine":1,"totalLines":102}}}
