{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01KWRdu3N61DRVwb8Hw7aAnf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env python3\n2\t\"\"\"Anchor ⇄ Gandalf integration — the two-stage runtime engine (v1, Wave 1).\n3\t\n4\tGive each Anchor project an honest \"what's really going on here\" read by invoking\n5\tthe **existing** Gandalf skill through Anchor's runner seam, then grading the\n6\tresult with Gandalf's **own** Tier-1 host. Anchor is integration glue only —\n7\tGandalf's reasoning + grading are never reimplemented here.\n8\t\n9\tThe flow is two stages, both injectable + STUBBED in tests (never real claude /\n10\treal node):\n11\t\n12\t  Stage A (model) — build a prompt = the Gandalf ``SKILL.md`` protocol (read from\n13\t    ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_SKILL_DIR``) + \"analyze the project at <folder> and emit ONLY\n14\t    the RAW draft JSON per ``runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`` as your final message;\n15\t    do NOT self-assign tiers/stamps\". Launched through ``job_runner`` /\n16\t    ``ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`` with ``cwd=folder``, ``--add-dir folder``, an\n17\t    ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_TIMEOUT`` (default 600s), and the forwarded env. The raw\n18\t    draft is recovered via ``job_runner.extract_assistant_text`` + parsing the\n19\t    last balanced top-level JSON object.\n20\t\n21\t  Stage B (host) — run ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD`` (default\n22\t    ``node \"<skilldir>/runtime/gandalf-run.mjs\"``) feeding the raw draft on stdin,\n23\t    capturing the GRADED ``advisor-output.json`` on stdout. ``node`` is an\n24\t    EXTERNAL CLI through a seam (like git/gh) — never a Python dep. A parse\n25\t    failure / non-zero exit / absent host is an honest **error run**\n26\t    (``ok:false``, ``reason``) — never fabricated, never raised to the caller,\n27\t    never crashes a render.\n28\t\n29\tStore layout (decision #3 — served artifacts MUST live at PROJECT ROOT because\n30\t``report_viewer.resolve_project_artifact`` hard-rejects any path under\n31\t``.anchor``):\n32\t\n33\t  <folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/report.md          (full rendered schema)\n34\t  <folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/exec-summary.md     (verdict + top findings/elevations)\n35\t  <folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/advisor-output.json (the graded schema, audit truth)\n36\t\n37\tThe internal INDEX lives at ``.anchor/projects/<id>/gandalf/index.json`` (read\n38\tdirectly by the GET endpoint, never via ``/artifact``), newest-first, stamped\n39\twith ``GANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION``, written under ``paths.WRITE_LOCK``.\n40\t\n41\tStdlib only. No third-party imports.\n42\t\"\"\"\n43\t\n44\timport json\n45\timport os\n46\timport subprocess\n47\timport time\n48\tfrom pathlib import Path\n49\t\n50\timport paths as _paths\n51\timport job_runner as _jr\n52\timport summarizer as _summarizer\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t# ── Constants / seams ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n56\t\n57\t#: Env var pointing at the on-disk Gandalf skill folder (its ``SKILL.md`` +\n58\t#: ``runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`` live here). Resolves BLOCKER B — ``/gandalf`` is\n59\t#: not auto-discoverable, so the protocol is read from this dir.\n60\tSKILL_DIR_ENV = \"ANCHOR_GANDALF_SKILL_DIR\"\n61\tDEFAULT_SKILL_DIR = r\"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\"\n62\t\n63\t#: Env var overriding the Stage-B host command. When unset, the default is\n64\t#: ``node \"<skilldir>/runtime/gandalf-run.mjs\"``. ``node`` is an external CLI\n65\t#: through a seam (like git/gh) — never a Python dep. Tests point this at a\n66\t#: Python stub emitting a canned graded advisor-output.json.\n67\tHOST_CMD_ENV = \"ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD\"\n68\t\n69\t#: Env var overriding the Stage-A model timeout (seconds). Pointing Gandalf at a\n70\t#: whole project folder is an unbounded agentic run, so this is GENEROUS and\n71\t#: Gandalf-specific — NOT summarizer's 60s. An honest degraded run on timeout,\n72\t#: never a hang.\n73\tTIMEOUT_ENV = \"ANCHOR_GANDALF_TIMEOUT\"\n74\tDEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 600.0\n75\t\n76\t#: Project-root subdir holding the served run artifacts (NOT under .anchor, which\n77\t#: /artifact rejects). One ``run-<ts>/`` per run.\n78\tGANDALF_DIRNAME = \"gandalf\"\n79\t\n80\t#: Internal index (under the per-project store) + its filenames. NEVER served via\n81\t#: /artifact — read directly by the GET endpoint.\n82\tINDEX_DIRNAME = \"gandalf\"\n83\tINDEX_FILENAME = \"index.json\"\n84\t\n85\t#: Per-run artifact filenames.\n86\tREPORT_MD = \"report.md\"\n87\tEXEC_SUMMARY_MD = \"exec-summary.md\"\n88\tADVISOR_OUTPUT_JSON = \"advisor-output.json\"\n89\t\n90\t#: Index schema version. BUMP when a fix changes what a correct index record\n91\t#: looks like; ``list_runs`` normalizes older/missing versions with honest\n92\t#: defaults so stale indexes don't crash the read path.\n93\tGANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION = 1\n94\t\n95\t#: The 9 required top-level keys of a graded advisor-output (per\n96\t#: ``schema/advisor-output.schema.json``). A graded output missing any of these\n97\t#: is a malformed host result → an honest error run.\n98\t_REQUIRED_TOP_KEYS = (\n99\t    \"schema_version\", \"cross_model\", \"degraded\", \"reasoning\", \"verdict\",\n100\t    \"findings\", \"nitpicks\", \"elevations\", \"risk_labels\",\n101\t)\n102\t\n103\t#: How many bytes of SKILL.md to embed in the Stage-A prompt (bounded).\n104\t_MAX_SKILL_BYTES = 64 * 1024\n105\t\n106\t\n107\t# ── Path helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n108\t\n109\tdef _skill_dir() -> Path:\n110\t    raw = (os.environ.get(SKILL_DIR_ENV) or \"\").strip() or DEFAULT_SKILL_DIR\n111\t    return Path(raw)\n112\t\n113\t\n114\tdef _timeout() -> float:\n115\t    raw = (os.environ.get(TIMEOUT_ENV) or \"\").strip()\n116\t    if not raw:\n117\t        return DEFAULT_TIMEOUT\n118\t    try:\n119\t        return float(raw)\n120\t    except ValueError:\n121\t        return DEFAULT_TIMEOUT\n122\t\n123\t\n124\tdef _runs_dir(folder_path) -> Path:\n125\t    \"\"\"``<folder>/gandalf/`` — the project-root dir holding run-<ts>/ subdirs.\"\"\"\n126\t    return Path(folder_path) / GANDALF_DIRNAME\n127\t\n128\t\n129\tdef _index_path(folder_path, project_id) -> Path:\n130\t    \"\"\"``<folder>/.anchor/projects/<id>/gandalf/index.json`` — the internal index.\"\"\"\n131\t    return (_summarizer._project_store_dir(folder_path, project_id)\n132\t            / INDEX_DIRNAME / INDEX_FILENAME)\n133\t\n134\t\n135\tdef _host_cmd_argv():\n136\t    \"\"\"Resolve the Stage-B host command as an argv list.\n137\t\n138\t    ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD`` wins (tests point it at a Python stub); else the\n139\t    default ``node \"<skilldir>/runtime/gandalf-run.mjs\"``. Split survives Windows\n140\t    backslash paths (reuses job_runner's splitter).\n141\t    \"\"\"\n142\t    override = (os.environ.get(HOST_CMD_ENV) or \"\").strip()\n143\t    if override:\n144\t        return _jr._shlex_split(override)\n145\t    host_mjs = _skill_dir() / \"runtime\" / \"gandalf-run.mjs\"\n146\t    return [\"node\", str(host_mjs)]\n147\t\n148\t\n149\t# ── Stage A — build the embedded-protocol prompt ─────────────────────────────\n150\t\n151\tdef _read_skill_protocol() -> str:\n152\t    \"\"\"Read ``SKILL.md`` from the skill dir (bounded). Honest empty on absence.\"\"\"\n153\t    try:\n154\t        p = _skill_dir() / \"SKILL.md\"\n155\t        if not p.is_file():\n156\t            return \"\"\n157\t        return p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")[:_MAX_SKILL_BYTES]\n158\t    except OSError:\n159\t        return \"\"\n160\t\n161\t\n162\tdef _build_prompt(folder_path) -> str:\n163\t    \"\"\"Stage-A prompt = the Gandalf protocol + the raw-draft instruction.\"\"\"\n164\t    protocol = _read_skill_protocol()\n165\t    parts = []\n166\t    if protocol:\n167\t        parts.append(\"You are running the Gandalf deep-think advisor skill. Its \"\n168\t                     \"protocol follows verbatim:\\n\\n\" + protocol)\n169\t    else:\n170\t        parts.append(\"You are running the Gandalf deep-think advisor skill.\")\n171\t    parts.append(\n172\t        \"Analyze the project at the following folder and emit ONLY the RAW draft \"\n173\t        \"JSON per the skill's runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md as your FINAL message. \"\n174\t        \"Do NOT self-assign tiers or refutation stamps — the host applies them.\\n\\n\"\n175\t        f\"Project folder: {folder_path}\")\n176\t    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)\n177\t\n178\t\n179\t# ── JSON extraction (last balanced top-level object) ─────────────────────────\n180\t\n181\tdef _last_balanced_json(text: str):\n182\t    \"\"\"Locate + parse the LAST balanced top-level JSON object in ``text``.\n183\t\n184\t    Scans for ``{`` ... matching ``}`` spans at brace-depth 0 (string/escape\n185\t    aware so braces inside strings don't confuse the depth count) and returns the\n186\t    parsed value of the LAST one that ``json.loads`` accepts. Returns ``None`` if\n187\t    none parse. Stdlib only; never raises.\n188\t    \"\"\"\n189\t    if not text:\n190\t        return None\n191\t    spans = []\n192\t    depth = 0\n193\t    start = -1\n194\t    in_str = False\n195\t    esc = False\n196\t    for i, ch in enumerate(text):\n197\t        if in_str:\n198\t            if esc:\n199\t                esc = False\n200\t            elif ch == \"\\\\\":\n201\t                esc = True\n202\t            elif ch == '\"':\n203\t                in_str = False\n204\t            continue\n205\t        if ch == '\"':\n206\t            in_str = True\n207\t            continue\n208\t        if ch == \"{\":\n209\t            if depth == 0:\n210\t                start = i\n211\t            depth += 1\n212\t        elif ch == \"}\":\n213\t            if depth > 0:\n214\t                depth -= 1\n215\t                if depth == 0 and start >= 0:\n216\t                    spans.append((start, i + 1))\n217\t                    start = -1\n218\t    for s, e in reversed(spans):\n219\t        try:\n220\t            obj = json.loads(text[s:e])\n221\t        except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n222\t            continue\n223\t        if isinstance(obj, dict):\n224\t            return obj\n225\t    return None\n226\t\n227\t\n228\t# ── Stage A — run the model, recover the raw draft ───────────────────────────\n229\t\n230\tdef _run_stage_a(folder_path, env=None):\n231\t    \"\"\"Run Stage A → ``(raw_draft_dict, reason)``.\n232\t\n233\t    On any failure (job failed/timed-out, no parseable JSON) returns\n234\t    ``(None, \"<reason>\")``. Never raises.\n235\t    \"\"\"\n236\t    folder = str(folder_path)\n237\t    prompt = _build_prompt(folder)\n238\t    try:\n239\t        # READ-ONLY: Gandalf is an advisor — it analyzes the project and emits its\n240\t        # read as the final message; it writes NO file. ``permission_mode=\"plan\"``\n241\t        # ensures claude can NEVER edit the analyzed project (acceptEdits would let\n242\t        # it). ``output_dir=folder`` grants READ access to explore the project.\n243\t        rec = _jr.launch(\"research\", cwd=folder, prompt=prompt,\n244\t                         output_dir=folder, env=(env or None),\n245\t                         permission_mode=\"plan\")\n246\t    except Exception:\n247\t        return None, \"launch-failed\"\n248\t    jid = rec[\"job_id\"]\n249\t    _jr.wait(jid, timeout=_timeout())\n250\t    final = _jr.load_record(jid) or {}\n251\t    if final.get(\"status\") != _jr.STATUS_DONE:\n252\t        return None, \"stage-a-run-failed:\" + str(final.get(\"status\") or \"unknown\")\n253\t    lines = _jr.all_lines(jid)\n254\t    text_lines = _jr.extract_assistant_text(lines)\n255\t    draft = _last_balanced_json(\"\\n\".join(text_lines))\n256\t    if not isinstance(draft, dict):\n257\t        return None, \"stage-a-unparseable-draft\"\n258\t    return draft, None\n259\t\n260\t\n261\t# ── Stage B — run the host, recover the graded output ────────────────────────\n262\t\n263\tdef _run_stage_b(raw_draft):\n264\t    \"\"\"Run Stage B (the host) on the raw draft → ``(graded_dict, reason)``.\n265\t\n266\t    Feeds the raw draft on stdin, captures the graded advisor-output.json on\n267\t    stdout. A non-zero exit / absent host / unparseable output is an honest\n268\t    error (returns ``(None, \"<reason>\")``). Never raises.\n269\t    \"\"\"\n270\t    argv = _host_cmd_argv()\n271\t    payload = json.dumps(raw_draft, ensure_ascii=False)\n272\t    try:\n273\t        proc = subprocess.run(\n274\t            argv,\n275\t            input=payload,\n276\t            capture_output=True,\n277\t            text=True,\n278\t            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n279\t            errors=\"replace\",\n280\t            timeout=_timeout(),\n281\t        )\n282\t    except FileNotFoundError:\n283\t        return None, \"host-unavailable\"\n284\t    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):\n285\t        return None, \"host-spawn-failed\"\n286\t    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n287\t        return None, \"host-timeout\"\n288\t    if proc.returncode != 0:\n289\t        err = (proc.stderr or \"\").strip().splitlines()\n290\t        reason = \"host-nonzero-exit\"\n291\t        if err:\n292\t            reason += \":\" + err[-1][:200]\n293\t        return None, reason\n294\t    graded = _last_balanced_json(proc.stdout or \"\")\n295\t    if not isinstance(graded, dict):\n296\t        return None, \"host-unparseable-output\"\n297\t    missing = [k for k in _REQUIRED_TOP_KEYS if k not in graded]\n298\t    if missing:\n299\t        return None, \"host-output-missing-keys:\" + \",\".join(missing)\n300\t    return graded, None\n301\t\n302\t\n303\t# ── Render helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n304\t\n305\tdef _one_line_verdict(graded) -> str:\n306\t    \"\"\"The cleaned one-line verdict (pinned to the top-level ``verdict`` field).\"\"\"\n307\t    if not isinstance(graded, dict):\n308\t        return \"\"\n309\t    verdict = graded.get(\"verdict\") or \"\"\n310\t    return _summarizer.short_summary_text(str(verdict))\n311\t\n312\t\n313\tdef _severity_rank(item) -> int:\n314\t    order = {\"critical\": 0, \"major\": 1, \"minor\": 2}\n315\t    return order.get(str((item or {}).get(\"severity\") or \"\").lower(), 3)\n316\t\n317\t\n318\tdef _render_full_report(graded, *, run_id=\"\", when=None) -> str:\n319\t    \"\"\"Render the full graded schema as readable markdown. Defensive .get().\"\"\"\n320\t    g = graded if isinstance(graded, dict) else {}\n321\t    lines = [\"# Gandalf read\"]\n322\t    if run_id:\n323\t        lines.append(\"\")\n324\t        lines.append(f\"> Run `{run_id}`\"\n325\t                     + (f\" · {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M', time.localtime(when))}\"\n326\t                        if when else \"\"))\n327\t    verdict = str(g.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n328\t    if verdict:\n329\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Verdict\", \"\", verdict]\n330\t    chips = []\n331\t    if g.get(\"degraded\"):\n332\t        chips.append(\"degraded\")\n333\t    chips.append(\"cross_model:\" + (\"true\" if g.get(\"cross_model\") else \"false\"))\n334\t    lines += [\"\", \"## Honesty\", \"\", \"- \" + \" · \".join(chips)]\n335\t    reasoning = str(g.get(\"reasoning\") or \"\").strip()\n336\t    if reasoning:\n337\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Reasoning\", \"\", reasoning]\n338\t\n339\t    findings = [f for f in (g.get(\"findings\") or []) if isinstance(f, dict)]\n340\t    if findings:\n341\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Findings\", \"\"]\n342\t        for f in sorted(findings, key=_severity_rank):\n343\t            sev = str(f.get(\"severity\") or \"\").strip()\n344\t            kind = str(f.get(\"kind\") or \"\").strip()\n345\t            rung = str(f.get(\"rung\") or \"\").strip()\n346\t            tag = \" · \".join(x for x in (kind, sev, rung) if x)\n347\t            fid = str(f.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n348\t            head = f\"- **{fid}**\" + (f\" ({tag})\" if tag else \"\")\n349\t            lines.append(head)\n350\t            v = str(f.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n351\t            if v:\n352\t                lines.append(f\"  - {v}\")\n353\t\n354\t    elevations = [e for e in (g.get(\"elevations\") or []) if isinstance(e, dict)]\n355\t    if elevations:\n356\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Elevations\", \"\"]\n357\t        for e in elevations:\n358\t            eid = str(e.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n359\t            tier = str(e.get(\"tier\") or \"\").strip()\n360\t            val = str(e.get(\"value_if_true\") or \"\").strip()\n361\t            tag = \" · \".join(x for x in (tier, val) if x)\n362\t            head = f\"- **{eid}**\" + (f\" ({tag})\" if tag else \"\")\n363\t            lines.append(head)\n364\t            v = str(e.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n365\t            if v:\n366\t                lines.append(f\"  - {v}\")\n367\t\n368\t    nitpicks = [n for n in (g.get(\"nitpicks\") or []) if isinstance(n, dict)]\n369\t    if nitpicks:\n370\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Nitpicks\", \"\"]\n371\t        for n in nitpicks:\n372\t            nid = str(n.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n373\t            v = str(n.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n374\t            lines.append(f\"- **{nid}** {v}\".rstrip())\n375\t\n376\t    risk = [r for r in (g.get(\"risk_labels\") or []) if isinstance(r, dict)]\n377\t    if risk:\n378\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Risk labels\", \"\"]\n379\t        for r in risk:\n380\t            leg = str(r.get(\"leg\") or \"\").strip()\n381\t            tier = str(r.get(\"tier\") or \"\").strip()\n382\t            lines.append(f\"- {leg}: {tier}\".rstrip())\n383\t\n384\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n385\t\n386\t\n387\tdef _render_exec_summary(graded, *, run_id=\"\", when=None) -> str:\n388\t    \"\"\"Render the executive summary: verdict + top findings-by-severity + top\n389\t    elevations. Defensive .get() everywhere.\"\"\"\n390\t    g = graded if isinstance(graded, dict) else {}\n391\t    lines = [\"# Gandalf — executive summary\"]\n392\t    if run_id:\n393\t        lines.append(\"\")\n394\t        lines.append(f\"> Run `{run_id}`\"\n395\t                     + (f\" · {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M', time.localtime(when))}\"\n396\t                        if when else \"\"))\n397\t    verdict = str(g.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n398\t    if verdict:\n399\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Verdict\", \"\", verdict]\n400\t    chips = []\n401\t    if g.get(\"degraded\"):\n402\t        chips.append(\"degraded\")\n403\t    chips.append(\"cross_model:\" + (\"true\" if g.get(\"cross_model\") else \"false\"))\n404\t    lines += [\"\", \"_\" + \" · \".join(chips) + \"_\"]\n405\t\n406\t    findings = [f for f in (g.get(\"findings\") or []) if isinstance(f, dict)]\n407\t    top = sorted(findings, key=_severity_rank)[:5]\n408\t    if top:\n409\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Top findings\", \"\"]\n410\t        for f in top:\n411\t            sev = str(f.get(\"severity\") or \"\").strip()\n412\t            fid = str(f.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n413\t            v = str(f.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n414\t            head = f\"- **{fid}**\" + (f\" ({sev})\" if sev else \"\")\n415\t            if v:\n416\t                head += f\" — {v}\"\n417\t            lines.append(head)\n418\t\n419\t    elevations = [e for e in (g.get(\"elevations\") or []) if isinstance(e, dict)][:5]\n420\t    if elevations:\n421\t        lines += [\"\", \"## Top elevations\", \"\"]\n422\t        for e in elevations:\n423\t            eid = str(e.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n424\t            v = str(e.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n425\t            head = f\"- **{eid}**\" + (f\" — {v}\" if v else \"\")\n426\t            lines.append(head)\n427\t\n428\t    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n429\t\n430\t\n431\t# ── Index store ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n432\t\n433\tdef _load_index(folder_path, project_id) -> list:\n434\t    \"\"\"Load the raw index list (newest-first). Honest empty on absence/corruption.\"\"\"\n435\t    p = _index_path(folder_path, project_id)\n436\t    if not p.exists():\n437\t        return []\n438\t    try:\n439\t        data = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n440\t    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n441\t        return []\n442\t    if isinstance(data, dict):\n443\t        data = data.get(\"runs\") or []\n444\t    if not isinstance(data, list):\n445\t        return []\n446\t    return [r for r in data if isinstance(r, dict)]\n447\t\n448\t\n449\tdef _append_index(folder_path, project_id, record: dict) -> None:\n450\t    \"\"\"Prepend a record (newest-first) to the index under the write lock.\"\"\"\n451\t    with _paths.WRITE_LOCK:\n452\t        p = _index_path(folder_path, project_id)\n453\t        p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n454\t        runs = _load_index(folder_path, project_id)\n455\t        runs.insert(0, record)\n456\t        tmp = p.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\")\n457\t        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(runs, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n458\t                       encoding=\"utf-8\")\n459\t        tmp.replace(p)\n460\t\n461\t\n462\tdef _add_gitignore_best_effort(folder_path) -> None:\n463\t    \"\"\"Best-effort: add ``gandalf/`` to the project ``.gitignore`` so regenerable\n464\t    analysis doesn't clutter git status. Never raises.\"\"\"\n465\t    try:\n466\t        gi = Path(folder_path) / \".gitignore\"\n467\t        existing = \"\"\n468\t        if gi.exists():\n469\t            existing = gi.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n470\t        lines = [ln.strip() for ln in existing.splitlines()]\n471\t        if \"gandalf/\" in lines or \"/gandalf/\" in lines or \"gandalf\" in lines:\n472\t            return\n473\t        sep = \"\" if (existing == \"\" or existing.endswith(\"\\n\")) else \"\\n\"\n474\t        with gi.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n475\t            fh.write(sep + \"gandalf/\\n\")\n476\t    except OSError:\n477\t        pass\n478\t\n479\t\n480\t# ── Public engine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n481\t\n482\tdef run_gandalf(folder_path, project_id, *, force=False, env=None) -> dict:\n483\t    \"\"\"Run one full two-stage Gandalf analysis and store the result.\n484\t\n485\t    Stage A (model, through ``ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD``) → the RAW draft → Stage B (the\n486\t    host, through ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD``) → the GRADED advisor-output. Render\n487\t    ``report.md`` + ``exec-summary.md``, write them + ``advisor-output.json`` to\n488\t    ``<folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/``, append a SAFE record to the internal index.\n489\t\n490\t    Returns a dict carrying at least ``{ok, run_id, ts, reason?}``. On a Stage-A\n491\t    or Stage-B failure an honest **error run** is recorded (``ok:false`` + a\n492\t    ``reason``, no fabricated verdict) and still appended to the index so the tab\n493\t    can show the honest failed row. NEVER raises to the caller. ``force`` is\n494\t    accepted for signature parity (every call is a fresh run — history accumulates).\n495\t    \"\"\"\n496\t    folder = str(folder_path)\n497\t    pid = str(project_id)\n498\t    ts = time.time()\n499\t    # A run id stable + filesystem-safe: run-<unix-ms>.\n500\t    run_id = \"run-\" + str(int(ts * 1000))\n501\t    run_rel = f\"{GANDALF_DIRNAME}/{run_id}\"\n502\t\n503\t    draft, reason = _run_stage_a(folder, env=env)\n504\t    graded = None\n505\t    if draft is not None:\n506\t        graded, reason = _run_stage_b(draft)\n507\t\n508\t    ok = graded is not None\n509\t\n510\t    report_rel = None\n511\t    exec_rel = None\n512\t    verdict = \"\"\n513\t    degraded = True\n514\t    cross_model = False\n515\t\n516\t    if ok:\n517\t        verdict = _one_line_verdict(graded)\n518\t        degraded = bool(graded.get(\"degraded\"))\n519\t        cross_model = bool(graded.get(\"cross_model\"))\n520\t        try:\n521\t            run_dir = _runs_dir(folder) / run_id\n522\t            run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n523\t            report_md = _render_full_report(graded, run_id=run_id, when=ts)\n524\t            exec_md = _render_exec_summary(graded, run_id=run_id, when=ts)\n525\t            (run_dir / REPORT_MD).write_text(report_md, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n526\t            (run_dir / EXEC_SUMMARY_MD).write_text(exec_md, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n527\t            (run_dir / ADVISOR_OUTPUT_JSON).write_text(\n528\t                json.dumps(graded, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n529\t                encoding=\"utf-8\")\n530\t            report_rel = f\"{run_rel}/{REPORT_MD}\"\n531\t            exec_rel = f\"{run_rel}/{EXEC_SUMMARY_MD}\"\n532\t            _add_gitignore_best_effort(folder)\n533\t        except OSError as exc:\n534\t            ok = False\n535\t            reason = \"artifact-write-failed:\" + str(exc)[:160]\n536\t            report_rel = None\n537\t            exec_rel = None\n538\t\n539\t    record = {\n540\t        \"schema_version\": GANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n541\t        \"run_id\": run_id,\n542\t        \"ts\": ts,\n543\t        \"ok\": bool(ok),\n544\t        \"verdict\": verdict,\n545\t        \"degraded\": bool(degraded),\n546\t        \"cross_model\": bool(cross_model),\n547\t        \"report_rel\": report_rel,\n548\t        \"exec_rel\": exec_rel,\n549\t        \"advisor_rel\": (f\"{run_rel}/{ADVISOR_OUTPUT_JSON}\" if ok else None),\n550\t    }\n551\t    if not ok:\n552\t        record[\"reason\"] = reason or \"unknown\"\n553\t\n554\t    try:\n555\t        _append_index(folder, pid, record)\n556\t    except Exception:\n557\t        # Even if the index write somehow fails, return the honest result.\n558\t        pass\n559\t\n560\t    out = dict(record)\n561\t    out[\"ok\"] = bool(ok)\n562\t    if not ok:\n563\t        out[\"reason\"] = reason or \"unknown\"\n564\t    return out\n565\t\n566\t\n567\tdef run_gandalf_if_absent(folder_path, project_id, env=None) -> dict:\n568\t    \"\"\"First-scan idempotent: run Gandalf ONLY if no prior run exists.\n569\t\n570\t    Returns ``{ok:True, skipped:True}`` when a prior run is present (no model\n571\t    call), else delegates to :func:`run_gandalf`. Never raises.\n572\t    \"\"\"\n573\t    try:\n574\t        if _load_index(folder_path, project_id):\n575\t            return {\"ok\": True, \"skipped\": True, \"reason\": \"prior-run-exists\"}\n576\t    except Exception:\n577\t        pass\n578\t    return run_gandalf(folder_path, project_id, env=env)\n579\t\n580\t\n581\t# ── Read seams (SAFE projections — never absolute paths) ─────────────────────\n582\t\n583\tdef _safe_run_view(record: dict) -> dict:\n584\t    \"\"\"SAFE projection of one index record (no absolute paths).\"\"\"\n585\t    r = record if isinstance(record, dict) else {}\n586\t    view = {\n587\t        \"run_id\": str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\"),\n588\t        \"ts\": r.get(\"ts\"),\n589\t        \"ok\": bool(r.get(\"ok\")),\n590\t        \"verdict\": str(r.get(\"verdict\") or \"\"),\n591\t        \"degraded\": bool(r.get(\"degraded\", True)),\n592\t        \"cross_model\": bool(r.get(\"cross_model\", False)),\n593\t        \"report_rel\": r.get(\"report_rel\"),\n594\t        \"exec_rel\": r.get(\"exec_rel\"),\n595\t        \"advisor_rel\": r.get(\"advisor_rel\"),\n596\t    }\n597\t    reason = r.get(\"reason\")\n598\t    if reason:\n599\t        view[\"reason\"] = str(reason)\n600\t    return view\n601\t\n602\t\n603\tdef list_runs(folder_path, project_id) -> list:\n604\t    \"\"\"Newest-first SAFE projections of the project's Gandalf runs.\n605\t\n606\t    Each: ``ts · run_id · verdict · cross_model · degraded · ok · report_rel ·\n607\t    exec_rel · advisor_rel · reason?`` — NEVER an absolute path. Normalizes\n608\t    older/missing-schema records with honest defaults. Read-only; never raises.\n609\t    \"\"\"\n610\t    runs = _load_index(folder_path, project_id)\n611\t    return [_safe_run_view(r) for r in runs]\n612\t\n613\t\n614\tdef get_run(folder_path, project_id, run_id) -> dict:\n615\t    \"\"\"The SAFE projection of one run by id, or ``None``. Read-only.\"\"\"\n616\t    for r in _load_index(folder_path, project_id):\n617\t        if str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\") == str(run_id):\n618\t            return _safe_run_view(r)\n619\t    return None\n620\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8879e2bf-702b-4c2f-a33b-7fb98e48e304","uuid":"d3c3798a-46fd-4fcf-bb14-21fa13670e4c","timestamp":"2026-06-23T18:33:41.202Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\dev\\Anchor\\gandalf.py","content":"#!/usr/bin/env python3\n\"\"\"Anchor ⇄ Gandalf integration — the two-stage runtime engine (v1, Wave 1).\n\nGive each Anchor project an honest \"what's really going on here\" read by invoking\nthe **existing** Gandalf skill through Anchor's runner seam, then grading the\nresult with Gandalf's **own** Tier-1 host. Anchor is integration glue only —\nGandalf's reasoning + grading are never reimplemented here.\n\nThe flow is two stages, both injectable + STUBBED in tests (never real claude /\nreal node):\n\n  Stage A (model) — build a prompt = the Gandalf ``SKILL.md`` protocol (read from\n    ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_SKILL_DIR``) + \"analyze the project at <folder> and emit ONLY\n    the RAW draft JSON per ``runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md`` as your final message;\n    do NOT self-assign tiers/stamps\". Launched through ``job_runner`` /\n    ``ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD`` with ``cwd=folder``, ``--add-dir folder``, an\n    ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_TIMEOUT`` (default 600s), and the forwarded env. The raw\n    draft is recovered via ``job_runner.extract_assistant_text`` + parsing the\n    last balanced top-level JSON object.\n\n  Stage B (host) — run ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD`` (default\n    ``node \"<skilldir>/runtime/gandalf-run.mjs\"``) feeding the raw draft on stdin,\n    capturing the GRADED ``advisor-output.json`` on stdout. ``node`` is an\n    EXTERNAL CLI through a seam (like git/gh) — never a Python dep. A parse\n    failure / non-zero exit / absent host is an honest **error run**\n    (``ok:false``, ``reason``) — never fabricated, never raised to the caller,\n    never crashes a render.\n\nStore layout (decision #3 — served artifacts MUST live at PROJECT ROOT because\n``report_viewer.resolve_project_artifact`` hard-rejects any path under\n``.anchor``):\n\n  <folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/report.md          (full rendered schema)\n  <folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/exec-summary.md     (verdict + top findings/elevations)\n  <folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/advisor-output.json (the graded schema, audit truth)\n\nThe internal INDEX lives at ``.anchor/projects/<id>/gandalf/index.json`` (read\ndirectly by the GET endpoint, never via ``/artifact``), newest-first, stamped\nwith ``GANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION``, written under ``paths.WRITE_LOCK``.\n\nStdlib only. No third-party imports.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport json\nimport os\nimport subprocess\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nimport paths as _paths\nimport job_runner as _jr\nimport summarizer as _summarizer\n\n\n# ── Constants / seams ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n#: Env var pointing at the on-disk Gandalf skill folder (its ``SKILL.md`` +\n#: ``runtime/gandalf-run.mjs`` live here). Resolves BLOCKER B — ``/gandalf`` is\n#: not auto-discoverable, so the protocol is read from this dir.\nSKILL_DIR_ENV = \"ANCHOR_GANDALF_SKILL_DIR\"\nDEFAULT_SKILL_DIR = r\"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\"\n\n#: Env var overriding the Stage-B host command. When unset, the default is\n#: ``node \"<skilldir>/runtime/gandalf-run.mjs\"``. ``node`` is an external CLI\n#: through a seam (like git/gh) — never a Python dep. Tests point this at a\n#: Python stub emitting a canned graded advisor-output.json.\nHOST_CMD_ENV = \"ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD\"\n\n#: Env var overriding the Stage-A model timeout (seconds). Pointing Gandalf at a\n#: whole project folder is an unbounded agentic run, so this is GENEROUS and\n#: Gandalf-specific — NOT summarizer's 60s. An honest degraded run on timeout,\n#: never a hang.\nTIMEOUT_ENV = \"ANCHOR_GANDALF_TIMEOUT\"\nDEFAULT_TIMEOUT = 600.0\n\n#: Project-root subdir holding the served run artifacts (NOT under .anchor, which\n#: /artifact rejects). One ``run-<ts>/`` per run.\nGANDALF_DIRNAME = \"gandalf\"\n\n#: Internal index (under the per-project store) + its filenames. NEVER served via\n#: /artifact — read directly by the GET endpoint.\nINDEX_DIRNAME = \"gandalf\"\nINDEX_FILENAME = \"index.json\"\n\n#: Per-run artifact filenames.\nREPORT_MD = \"report.md\"\nEXEC_SUMMARY_MD = \"exec-summary.md\"\nADVISOR_OUTPUT_JSON = \"advisor-output.json\"\n\n#: Index schema version. BUMP when a fix changes what a correct index record\n#: looks like; ``list_runs`` normalizes older/missing versions with honest\n#: defaults so stale indexes don't crash the read path.\nGANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION = 1\n\n#: The 9 required top-level keys of a graded advisor-output (per\n#: ``schema/advisor-output.schema.json``). A graded output missing any of these\n#: is a malformed host result → an honest error run.\n_REQUIRED_TOP_KEYS = (\n    \"schema_version\", \"cross_model\", \"degraded\", \"reasoning\", \"verdict\",\n    \"findings\", \"nitpicks\", \"elevations\", \"risk_labels\",\n)\n\n#: How many bytes of SKILL.md to embed in the Stage-A prompt (bounded).\n_MAX_SKILL_BYTES = 64 * 1024\n\n\n# ── Path helpers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _skill_dir() -> Path:\n    raw = (os.environ.get(SKILL_DIR_ENV) or \"\").strip() or DEFAULT_SKILL_DIR\n    return Path(raw)\n\n\ndef _timeout() -> float:\n    raw = (os.environ.get(TIMEOUT_ENV) or \"\").strip()\n    if not raw:\n        return DEFAULT_TIMEOUT\n    try:\n        return float(raw)\n    except ValueError:\n        return DEFAULT_TIMEOUT\n\n\ndef _runs_dir(folder_path) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"``<folder>/gandalf/`` — the project-root dir holding run-<ts>/ subdirs.\"\"\"\n    return Path(folder_path) / GANDALF_DIRNAME\n\n\ndef _index_path(folder_path, project_id) -> Path:\n    \"\"\"``<folder>/.anchor/projects/<id>/gandalf/index.json`` — the internal index.\"\"\"\n    return (_summarizer._project_store_dir(folder_path, project_id)\n            / INDEX_DIRNAME / INDEX_FILENAME)\n\n\ndef _host_cmd_argv():\n    \"\"\"Resolve the Stage-B host command as an argv list.\n\n    ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD`` wins (tests point it at a Python stub); else the\n    default ``node \"<skilldir>/runtime/gandalf-run.mjs\"``. Split survives Windows\n    backslash paths (reuses job_runner's splitter).\n    \"\"\"\n    override = (os.environ.get(HOST_CMD_ENV) or \"\").strip()\n    if override:\n        return _jr._shlex_split(override)\n    host_mjs = _skill_dir() / \"runtime\" / \"gandalf-run.mjs\"\n    return [\"node\", str(host_mjs)]\n\n\n# ── Stage A — build the embedded-protocol prompt ─────────────────────────────\n\ndef _read_skill_protocol() -> str:\n    \"\"\"Read ``SKILL.md`` from the skill dir (bounded). Honest empty on absence.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        p = _skill_dir() / \"SKILL.md\"\n        if not p.is_file():\n            return \"\"\n        return p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")[:_MAX_SKILL_BYTES]\n    except OSError:\n        return \"\"\n\n\ndef _build_prompt(folder_path) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Stage-A prompt = the Gandalf protocol + the raw-draft instruction.\"\"\"\n    protocol = _read_skill_protocol()\n    parts = []\n    if protocol:\n        parts.append(\"You are running the Gandalf deep-think advisor skill. Its \"\n                     \"protocol follows verbatim:\\n\\n\" + protocol)\n    else:\n        parts.append(\"You are running the Gandalf deep-think advisor skill.\")\n    parts.append(\n        \"Analyze the project at the following folder and emit ONLY the RAW draft \"\n        \"JSON per the skill's runtime/RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md as your FINAL message. \"\n        \"Do NOT self-assign tiers or refutation stamps — the host applies them.\\n\\n\"\n        f\"Project folder: {folder_path}\")\n    return \"\\n\\n\".join(parts)\n\n\n# ── JSON extraction (last balanced top-level object) ─────────────────────────\n\ndef _last_balanced_json(text: str):\n    \"\"\"Locate + parse the LAST balanced top-level JSON object in ``text``.\n\n    Scans for ``{`` ... matching ``}`` spans at brace-depth 0 (string/escape\n    aware so braces inside strings don't confuse the depth count) and returns the\n    parsed value of the LAST one that ``json.loads`` accepts. Returns ``None`` if\n    none parse. Stdlib only; never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not text:\n        return None\n    spans = []\n    depth = 0\n    start = -1\n    in_str = False\n    esc = False\n    for i, ch in enumerate(text):\n        if in_str:\n            if esc:\n                esc = False\n            elif ch == \"\\\\\":\n                esc = True\n            elif ch == '\"':\n                in_str = False\n            continue\n        if ch == '\"':\n            in_str = True\n            continue\n        if ch == \"{\":\n            if depth == 0:\n                start = i\n            depth += 1\n        elif ch == \"}\":\n            if depth > 0:\n                depth -= 1\n                if depth == 0 and start >= 0:\n                    spans.append((start, i + 1))\n                    start = -1\n    for s, e in reversed(spans):\n        try:\n            obj = json.loads(text[s:e])\n        except (json.JSONDecodeError, ValueError):\n            continue\n        if isinstance(obj, dict):\n            return obj\n    return None\n\n\n# ── Stage A — run the model, recover the raw draft ───────────────────────────\n\ndef _run_stage_a(folder_path, env=None):\n    \"\"\"Run Stage A → ``(raw_draft_dict, reason)``.\n\n    On any failure (job failed/timed-out, no parseable JSON) returns\n    ``(None, \"<reason>\")``. Never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    folder = str(folder_path)\n    prompt = _build_prompt(folder)\n    try:\n        # READ-ONLY: Gandalf is an advisor — it analyzes the project and emits its\n        # read as the final message; it writes NO file. ``permission_mode=\"plan\"``\n        # ensures claude can NEVER edit the analyzed project (acceptEdits would let\n        # it). ``output_dir=folder`` grants READ access to explore the project.\n        rec = _jr.launch(\"research\", cwd=folder, prompt=prompt,\n                         output_dir=folder, env=(env or None),\n                         permission_mode=\"plan\")\n    except Exception:\n        return None, \"launch-failed\"\n    jid = rec[\"job_id\"]\n    _jr.wait(jid, timeout=_timeout())\n    final = _jr.load_record(jid) or {}\n    if final.get(\"status\") != _jr.STATUS_DONE:\n        return None, \"stage-a-run-failed:\" + str(final.get(\"status\") or \"unknown\")\n    lines = _jr.all_lines(jid)\n    text_lines = _jr.extract_assistant_text(lines)\n    draft = _last_balanced_json(\"\\n\".join(text_lines))\n    if not isinstance(draft, dict):\n        return None, \"stage-a-unparseable-draft\"\n    return draft, None\n\n\n# ── Stage B — run the host, recover the graded output ────────────────────────\n\ndef _run_stage_b(raw_draft):\n    \"\"\"Run Stage B (the host) on the raw draft → ``(graded_dict, reason)``.\n\n    Feeds the raw draft on stdin, captures the graded advisor-output.json on\n    stdout. A non-zero exit / absent host / unparseable output is an honest\n    error (returns ``(None, \"<reason>\")``). Never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    argv = _host_cmd_argv()\n    payload = json.dumps(raw_draft, ensure_ascii=False)\n    try:\n        proc = subprocess.run(\n            argv,\n            input=payload,\n            capture_output=True,\n            text=True,\n            encoding=\"utf-8\",\n            errors=\"replace\",\n            timeout=_timeout(),\n        )\n    except FileNotFoundError:\n        return None, \"host-unavailable\"\n    except (OSError, subprocess.SubprocessError):\n        return None, \"host-spawn-failed\"\n    except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:\n        return None, \"host-timeout\"\n    if proc.returncode != 0:\n        err = (proc.stderr or \"\").strip().splitlines()\n        reason = \"host-nonzero-exit\"\n        if err:\n            reason += \":\" + err[-1][:200]\n        return None, reason\n    graded = _last_balanced_json(proc.stdout or \"\")\n    if not isinstance(graded, dict):\n        return None, \"host-unparseable-output\"\n    missing = [k for k in _REQUIRED_TOP_KEYS if k not in graded]\n    if missing:\n        return None, \"host-output-missing-keys:\" + \",\".join(missing)\n    return graded, None\n\n\n# ── Render helpers ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _one_line_verdict(graded) -> str:\n    \"\"\"The cleaned one-line verdict (pinned to the top-level ``verdict`` field).\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(graded, dict):\n        return \"\"\n    verdict = graded.get(\"verdict\") or \"\"\n    return _summarizer.short_summary_text(str(verdict))\n\n\ndef _severity_rank(item) -> int:\n    order = {\"critical\": 0, \"major\": 1, \"minor\": 2}\n    return order.get(str((item or {}).get(\"severity\") or \"\").lower(), 3)\n\n\ndef _render_full_report(graded, *, run_id=\"\", when=None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Render the full graded schema as readable markdown. Defensive .get().\"\"\"\n    g = graded if isinstance(graded, dict) else {}\n    lines = [\"# Gandalf read\"]\n    if run_id:\n        lines.append(\"\")\n        lines.append(f\"> Run `{run_id}`\"\n                     + (f\" · {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M', time.localtime(when))}\"\n                        if when else \"\"))\n    verdict = str(g.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n    if verdict:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Verdict\", \"\", verdict]\n    chips = []\n    if g.get(\"degraded\"):\n        chips.append(\"degraded\")\n    chips.append(\"cross_model:\" + (\"true\" if g.get(\"cross_model\") else \"false\"))\n    lines += [\"\", \"## Honesty\", \"\", \"- \" + \" · \".join(chips)]\n    reasoning = str(g.get(\"reasoning\") or \"\").strip()\n    if reasoning:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Reasoning\", \"\", reasoning]\n\n    findings = [f for f in (g.get(\"findings\") or []) if isinstance(f, dict)]\n    if findings:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Findings\", \"\"]\n        for f in sorted(findings, key=_severity_rank):\n            sev = str(f.get(\"severity\") or \"\").strip()\n            kind = str(f.get(\"kind\") or \"\").strip()\n            rung = str(f.get(\"rung\") or \"\").strip()\n            tag = \" · \".join(x for x in (kind, sev, rung) if x)\n            fid = str(f.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n            head = f\"- **{fid}**\" + (f\" ({tag})\" if tag else \"\")\n            lines.append(head)\n            v = str(f.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n            if v:\n                lines.append(f\"  - {v}\")\n\n    elevations = [e for e in (g.get(\"elevations\") or []) if isinstance(e, dict)]\n    if elevations:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Elevations\", \"\"]\n        for e in elevations:\n            eid = str(e.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n            tier = str(e.get(\"tier\") or \"\").strip()\n            val = str(e.get(\"value_if_true\") or \"\").strip()\n            tag = \" · \".join(x for x in (tier, val) if x)\n            head = f\"- **{eid}**\" + (f\" ({tag})\" if tag else \"\")\n            lines.append(head)\n            v = str(e.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n            if v:\n                lines.append(f\"  - {v}\")\n\n    nitpicks = [n for n in (g.get(\"nitpicks\") or []) if isinstance(n, dict)]\n    if nitpicks:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Nitpicks\", \"\"]\n        for n in nitpicks:\n            nid = str(n.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n            v = str(n.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n            lines.append(f\"- **{nid}** {v}\".rstrip())\n\n    risk = [r for r in (g.get(\"risk_labels\") or []) if isinstance(r, dict)]\n    if risk:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Risk labels\", \"\"]\n        for r in risk:\n            leg = str(r.get(\"leg\") or \"\").strip()\n            tier = str(r.get(\"tier\") or \"\").strip()\n            lines.append(f\"- {leg}: {tier}\".rstrip())\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n\n\ndef _render_exec_summary(graded, *, run_id=\"\", when=None) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Render the executive summary: verdict + top findings-by-severity + top\n    elevations. Defensive .get() everywhere.\"\"\"\n    g = graded if isinstance(graded, dict) else {}\n    lines = [\"# Gandalf — executive summary\"]\n    if run_id:\n        lines.append(\"\")\n        lines.append(f\"> Run `{run_id}`\"\n                     + (f\" · {time.strftime('%Y-%m-%d %H:%M', time.localtime(when))}\"\n                        if when else \"\"))\n    verdict = str(g.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n    if verdict:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Verdict\", \"\", verdict]\n    chips = []\n    if g.get(\"degraded\"):\n        chips.append(\"degraded\")\n    chips.append(\"cross_model:\" + (\"true\" if g.get(\"cross_model\") else \"false\"))\n    lines += [\"\", \"_\" + \" · \".join(chips) + \"_\"]\n\n    findings = [f for f in (g.get(\"findings\") or []) if isinstance(f, dict)]\n    top = sorted(findings, key=_severity_rank)[:5]\n    if top:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Top findings\", \"\"]\n        for f in top:\n            sev = str(f.get(\"severity\") or \"\").strip()\n            fid = str(f.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n            v = str(f.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n            head = f\"- **{fid}**\" + (f\" ({sev})\" if sev else \"\")\n            if v:\n                head += f\" — {v}\"\n            lines.append(head)\n\n    elevations = [e for e in (g.get(\"elevations\") or []) if isinstance(e, dict)][:5]\n    if elevations:\n        lines += [\"\", \"## Top elevations\", \"\"]\n        for e in elevations:\n            eid = str(e.get(\"id\") or \"\").strip()\n            v = str(e.get(\"verdict\") or \"\").strip()\n            head = f\"- **{eid}**\" + (f\" — {v}\" if v else \"\")\n            lines.append(head)\n\n    return \"\\n\".join(lines) + \"\\n\"\n\n\n# ── Index store ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef _load_index(folder_path, project_id) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Load the raw index list (newest-first). Honest empty on absence/corruption.\"\"\"\n    p = _index_path(folder_path, project_id)\n    if not p.exists():\n        return []\n    try:\n        data = json.loads(p.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"))\n    except (json.JSONDecodeError, OSError):\n        return []\n    if isinstance(data, dict):\n        data = data.get(\"runs\") or []\n    if not isinstance(data, list):\n        return []\n    return [r for r in data if isinstance(r, dict)]\n\n\ndef _append_index(folder_path, project_id, record: dict) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Prepend a record (newest-first) to the index under the write lock.\"\"\"\n    with _paths.WRITE_LOCK:\n        p = _index_path(folder_path, project_id)\n        p.parent.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        runs = _load_index(folder_path, project_id)\n        runs.insert(0, record)\n        tmp = p.with_suffix(\".json.tmp\")\n        tmp.write_text(json.dumps(runs, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n                       encoding=\"utf-8\")\n        tmp.replace(p)\n\n\ndef _add_gitignore_best_effort(folder_path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Best-effort: add ``gandalf/`` to the project ``.gitignore`` so regenerable\n    analysis doesn't clutter git status. Never raises.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        gi = Path(folder_path) / \".gitignore\"\n        existing = \"\"\n        if gi.exists():\n            existing = gi.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        lines = [ln.strip() for ln in existing.splitlines()]\n        if \"gandalf/\" in lines or \"/gandalf/\" in lines or \"gandalf\" in lines:\n            return\n        sep = \"\" if (existing == \"\" or existing.endswith(\"\\n\")) else \"\\n\"\n        with gi.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            fh.write(sep + \"gandalf/\\n\")\n    except OSError:\n        pass\n\n\n# ── Public engine ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\ndef run_gandalf(folder_path, project_id, *, force=False, env=None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"Run one full two-stage Gandalf analysis and store the result.\n\n    Stage A (model, through ``ANCHOR_RUNNER_CMD``) → the RAW draft → Stage B (the\n    host, through ``ANCHOR_GANDALF_HOST_CMD``) → the GRADED advisor-output. Render\n    ``report.md`` + ``exec-summary.md``, write them + ``advisor-output.json`` to\n    ``<folder>/gandalf/run-<ts>/``, append a SAFE record to the internal index.\n\n    Returns a dict carrying at least ``{ok, run_id, ts, reason?}``. On a Stage-A\n    or Stage-B failure an honest **error run** is recorded (``ok:false`` + a\n    ``reason``, no fabricated verdict) and still appended to the index so the tab\n    can show the honest failed row. NEVER raises to the caller. ``force`` is\n    accepted for signature parity (every call is a fresh run — history accumulates).\n    \"\"\"\n    folder = str(folder_path)\n    pid = str(project_id)\n    ts = time.time()\n    # A run id stable + filesystem-safe: run-<unix-ms>.\n    run_id = \"run-\" + str(int(ts * 1000))\n    run_rel = f\"{GANDALF_DIRNAME}/{run_id}\"\n\n    draft, reason = _run_stage_a(folder, env=env)\n    graded = None\n    if draft is not None:\n        graded, reason = _run_stage_b(draft)\n\n    ok = graded is not None\n\n    report_rel = None\n    exec_rel = None\n    verdict = \"\"\n    degraded = True\n    cross_model = False\n\n    if ok:\n        verdict = _one_line_verdict(graded)\n        degraded = bool(graded.get(\"degraded\"))\n        cross_model = bool(graded.get(\"cross_model\"))\n        try:\n            run_dir = _runs_dir(folder) / run_id\n            run_dir.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n            report_md = _render_full_report(graded, run_id=run_id, when=ts)\n            exec_md = _render_exec_summary(graded, run_id=run_id, when=ts)\n            (run_dir / REPORT_MD).write_text(report_md, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            (run_dir / EXEC_SUMMARY_MD).write_text(exec_md, encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            (run_dir / ADVISOR_OUTPUT_JSON).write_text(\n                json.dumps(graded, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False),\n                encoding=\"utf-8\")\n            report_rel = f\"{run_rel}/{REPORT_MD}\"\n            exec_rel = f\"{run_rel}/{EXEC_SUMMARY_MD}\"\n            _add_gitignore_best_effort(folder)\n        except OSError as exc:\n            ok = False\n            reason = \"artifact-write-failed:\" + str(exc)[:160]\n            report_rel = None\n            exec_rel = None\n\n    record = {\n        \"schema_version\": GANDALF_INDEX_SCHEMA_VERSION,\n        \"run_id\": run_id,\n        \"ts\": ts,\n        \"ok\": bool(ok),\n        \"verdict\": verdict,\n        \"degraded\": bool(degraded),\n        \"cross_model\": bool(cross_model),\n        \"report_rel\": report_rel,\n        \"exec_rel\": exec_rel,\n        \"advisor_rel\": (f\"{run_rel}/{ADVISOR_OUTPUT_JSON}\" if ok else None),\n    }\n    if not ok:\n        record[\"reason\"] = reason or \"unknown\"\n\n    try:\n        _append_index(folder, pid, record)\n    except Exception:\n        # Even if the index write somehow fails, return the honest result.\n        pass\n\n    out = dict(record)\n    out[\"ok\"] = bool(ok)\n    if not ok:\n        out[\"reason\"] = reason or \"unknown\"\n    return out\n\n\ndef run_gandalf_if_absent(folder_path, project_id, env=None) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"First-scan idempotent: run Gandalf ONLY if no prior run exists.\n\n    Returns ``{ok:True, skipped:True}`` when a prior run is present (no model\n    call), else delegates to :func:`run_gandalf`. Never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    try:\n        if _load_index(folder_path, project_id):\n            return {\"ok\": True, \"skipped\": True, \"reason\": \"prior-run-exists\"}\n    except Exception:\n        pass\n    return run_gandalf(folder_path, project_id, env=env)\n\n\n# ── Read seams (SAFE projections — never absolute paths) ─────────────────────\n\ndef _safe_run_view(record: dict) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"SAFE projection of one index record (no absolute paths).\"\"\"\n    r = record if isinstance(record, dict) else {}\n    view = {\n        \"run_id\": str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\"),\n        \"ts\": r.get(\"ts\"),\n        \"ok\": bool(r.get(\"ok\")),\n        \"verdict\": str(r.get(\"verdict\") or \"\"),\n        \"degraded\": bool(r.get(\"degraded\", True)),\n        \"cross_model\": bool(r.get(\"cross_model\", False)),\n        \"report_rel\": r.get(\"report_rel\"),\n        \"exec_rel\": r.get(\"exec_rel\"),\n        \"advisor_rel\": r.get(\"advisor_rel\"),\n    }\n    reason = r.get(\"reason\")\n    if reason:\n        view[\"reason\"] = str(reason)\n    return view\n\n\ndef list_runs(folder_path, project_id) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Newest-first SAFE projections of the project's Gandalf runs.\n\n    Each: ``ts · run_id · verdict · cross_model · degraded · ok · report_rel ·\n    exec_rel · advisor_rel · reason?`` — NEVER an absolute path. Normalizes\n    older/missing-schema records with honest defaults. Read-only; never raises.\n    \"\"\"\n    runs = _load_index(folder_path, project_id)\n    return [_safe_run_view(r) for r in runs]\n\n\ndef get_run(folder_path, project_id, run_id) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"The SAFE projection of one run by id, or ``None``. Read-only.\"\"\"\n    for r in _load_index(folder_path, project_id):\n        if str(r.get(\"run_id\") or \"\") == str(run_id):\n            return _safe_run_view(r)\n    return None\n","numLines":620,"startLine":1,"totalLines":620}}}
