iles; a 21,165-word CLAUDE.md; initial commit 2026-05-02 and HEAD 2026-06-23, i.e. TWELVE sequential 'R&D Control Surface' versions plus v10.1/v11.1/Gandalf in ~7 weeks. Today's healthcheck is GREEN on every surface. The deep structure: a project framed as 'a personal productivity system' whose artifact is now ~90% an agent-orchestration IDE (Mission Control for the researchPrime->Crucible->Foreman trio), with the original task/inbox/domain core apparently static since early May. The engineering discipline is unusually high (frozen plans, adversarial waves, worktree-only test lesson, permanent stubbed healthcheck guards, stdlib-only with one declared native exception). The central question is therefore NOT correctness (it is green and well-tested) but whether an ever-extending, self-built platform with no terminal objective and growing comprehension load remains sustainable for one person. I reason to verdict before stating it, and I deliberately ran a verdict-inverting reading (below) that genuinely tempers the drift critique without erasing it.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"This is sound and impressively disciplined as a working system, but it is drifting from its stated identity into an open-ended, self-built platform with no defined 'done', a heavy and version-stratified comprehension load, and at least one real production-data hygiene leak. Keep it — but set a stopping condition and a consolidation budget before the next version.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-identity-drift\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The README/CLAUDE.md North Star is 'Anchor - Productivity System for J.C. Liechty', but the observed artifact is overwhelmingly an R&D agent-orchestration platform: 261 api/rnd endpoints vs a handful of task endpoints, the four largest modules are all R&D-surface, and the productivity core (DASHBOARD.md task dates) appears static since ~2026-05-07 while v2..v12 + Gandalf were built. Critically, each version has its OWN planning/rnd-vN/MASTER-PLAN, but there is no single objective statement governing what the R&D surface as a whole is FOR or when it is DONE. Twelve versions in seven weeks with no terminal objective is an open-ended build with no stopping condition. This is the verdict-inverting candidate AND the operator-wrong finding: the operator's evident preference is to keep shipping versions; the finding is that the ABSENCE of a done-definition is itself the top risk, which runs against that preference.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"The artifact no longer matches its stated North Star, and the R&D surface has no overarching objective or definition-of-done; this is the single most consequential issue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-version-strata\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Every version 'EXTENDS existing seams' rather than consolidating them, so core modules now carry 6-10 layered generations of concern: terminal_session.py 3,170 LOC, effort_history.py 3,115, summarizer.py 1,894, and anchor_gui.py a 15,302-LOC single file mixing HTML/CSS/JS-in-f-strings/HTTP-handlers/change-ops. The 21k-word CLAUDE.md documents each version's seam-deltas in extraordinary prose detail and is effectively the only map of the system. The build is correct and green, but it is increasingly legible only through its own changelog -- a comprehension/maintenance debt that compounds per version.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Accumulating version strata on the same seams/files is a real and compounding comprehension cost, independent of current correctness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-registry-pollution\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The CLAUDE.md's most-repeated safety invariant is that every test/healthcheck uses temp dirs torn down afterward and 'never touches the real registry/:8777'. Yet the LIVE rnd_registry.json contains ~20 retired temp-folder 'projects' (C:\\\\Users\\\\john\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\tmp...\\\\test) AND >=3 ACTIVE temp leftovers ('S','P','I'), plus 5 duplicate same-folder 'Anchor' entries. This is direct evidence the temp-isolation invariant has been violated historically (manual runs and/or a pre-guard surface wrote the production registry), and the v2 reconcile_folder / v9 ghost-cleanup+dedup machinery built for exactly this is evidently not being run. rnd_jobs/ also holds 2,712 records with no retention policy.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"The production registry is polluted with test scaffolding and duplicates; the invariant that protects it has leaked, and the existing cleanup tools are unused.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-gui-monolith\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The documented 'how to add a feature' path routes nearly all UI/HTTP/change logic through one 15,302-LOC file, with JS/CSS embedded in Python f-strings (the CLAUDE.md flags the recurring pitfall: every literal brace must be doubled). The project ALREADY vendors static assets (xterm, anchor-term, brand), so the templating-in-f-string fragility is avoidable. The Playwright/DOM gate contains it today, but the correctness surface of 15k LOC of brace-escaped template strings is large and fragile.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"anchor_gui.py is a single-file monolith with an avoidable f-string-templating fragility class.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-doc-memory-drift\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The injected CLAUDE.md/persistent memory states v12 'Efforts' is 'NOT merged/deployed -- awaiting John's whole-branch sign-off', but git HEAD on master shows '7c2f51f Merge v12 Efforts to master' and 'bd153e7 Merge Gandalf integration v1', i.e. both are merged and