: \"situate\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"S0 abstraction (domain-neutral): 'a self-maintained system whose tooling layer grows until it absorbs and outpaces the original payload, with no terminal objective governing the tooling layer.' SITUATE fires (central load-bearing claim = a single operator can sustainably run an ever-extending self-built platform; a plausible better-in-class frame exists; stakes >= medium), but per protocol I do NOT self-verify: the relevant best-in-class frames -- internal-platform/framework accretion, the second-system effect, product-vs-platform boundary discipline, explicit definition-of-done / sunset criteria, and complexity-science views of unbounded accretion -- are a needs_verification handoff to researchPrime (no researchPrime ran on this single-family Tier-1 pass). The candidate structure-map (>=2 relational correspondences, asserted, UNVERIFIED): (1) the per-version 'EXTENDS existing seams with no retirement' maps to framework strata that are never deprecated; (2) 'green healthcheck per version but rising changelog-dependence' maps to test-coverage masking architectural entropy. Stated honestly as a frame to investigate, not a verified prescription.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SITUATE handoff: the 'tooling-eats-the-mission / no-sunset-criteria' pattern is well-studied in engineering and complexity literature; commission researchPrime to verify the best-in-class framing before relying on it. UNVERIFIED here.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nitpicks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n-mojibake\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"health_reports/2026-06-23.md renders em-dashes/checkmarks as mojibake (e.g. 'Anchor Health Report â€”', 'âœ“') despite the just-committed aa19ab1 'capture stdout as UTF-8 (fix Windows mojibake)'. The encoding fix evidently did not cover the health-report writer's output path.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Windows encoding fragility persists in the health-report writer; low stakes but recurring.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n-rnd-jobs-unbounded\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"rnd_jobs/ holds 2,712 job records. The 2026-06-16 perf fix made the dashboard hot path O(1) via targeted load_record, but the directory itself has no retention/rotation -- it only ever grows.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"rnd_jobs/ growth is now off the hot path but still unbounded on disk.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"elevations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-define-done\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"high\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Write ONE North Star + explicit definition-of-done / sunset criteria for the R&D control surface as a whole (not per-version), and adopt a consolidation budget: for the next N versions, every new version must retire or merge at least one prior stratum. This directly attacks d-identity-drift and a-comprehension-wall by replacing 'keep adding versions' with a measurable stopping/consolidation condition.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Set a terminal objective and a 'retire one stratum per new version' budget before v13.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If John's actual goal is open-ended R&D as a craft/practice -- the building IS the point, not a shippable end-state -- then a definition-of-done is a category error that imposes false closure on a deliberately unbounded project, and the right move is to drop the productivity-system framing instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-clean-registry\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"high\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Run the EXISTING v2 reconcile_folder + v9 ghost/cleanup machinery against the live registry now to drop the ~20 temp scaffolds and 5 duplicate Anchor entries; close the temp-pollution leak at its source (prove no surface walk can write the real registry, e.g. assert ANCHOR_DATA_DIR isolation in the offending path); and add a retention/rotation policy to rnd_jobs/. Addresses d-registry-pollution and a-registry-misact using tools already built.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Use the cleanup tools you already shipped, then seal the leak and bound rnd_jobs/.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If the temp/duplicate entries are provably inert everywhere (filtered out of all renders and all destructive ops the way __healthcheck__ is), and the move/push paths re-validate folder_path against disk before acting, then the pollution is cosmetic and the cleanup is unjustified churn.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-gandalf-livesmoke-gate\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Before depending on Gandalf in prod, perform the one-time real claude -p live-smoke from the deploy checklist and keep the first-scan auto-run OFF (or gated behind that smoke passing) until the live two-stage chain is proven to emit parseable schema within the 600s timeout. Addresses a-gandalf-never-worked-live without weakening the stubbed CI gate.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Prove the Gandalf live path once with real claude before enabling auto-run.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If _PROACTIVE_SUMMARY_ENABLED stays off in prod so no auto-run ever fires and Gandalf is only invoked manually (where an honest error row is immediately visible), the existing manual smoke is sufficient and a gate adds nothing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-extract-gui-assets\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Extract the anchor_gui.py JS/CSS out of Python f-strings into static vendored assets (you already serve vendor/xterm, vendor/anchor-term, vendor/brand via traversal-safe routes), eliminating the brace-doubling fragility class and shrinking the 15.3k-LOC monolith. Addresses d-gui-monolith.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Move embedded JS/CSS to vendored static files to kill the f-string brace hazard and shrink the monolith.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If f-string templating has caused zero shipped UI defects across v2..v12 (the brace-doubling discipline + Playwright gate fully contain it), the extraction is churn against a non-problem and risks introducing the very regressions it aims to prevent.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_read_input_tokens":133813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8879e2bf-702b-4c2f-a33b-7fb98e48e304","uuid":"e98e7e7e-e531-471e-aa43-a24b320980ae","request_id":"req_011CcLg3ct8jUgXqaMCbDpeA"}
