ck surface walks (v2..v12 + Gandalf); 164 test files; a 21,165-word CLAUDE.md; initial commit 2026-05-02 and HEAD 2026-06-23, i.e. TWELVE sequential 'R&D Control Surface' versions plus v10.1/v11.1/Gandalf in ~7 weeks. Today's healthcheck is GREEN on every surface. The deep structure: a project framed as 'a personal productivity system' whose artifact is now ~90% an agent-orchestration IDE (Mission Control for the researchPrime->Crucible->Foreman trio), with the original task/inbox/domain core apparently static since early May. The engineering discipline is unusually high (frozen plans, adversarial waves, worktree-only test lesson, permanent stubbed healthcheck guards, stdlib-only with one declared native exception). The central question is therefore NOT correctness (it is green and well-tested) but whether an ever-extending, self-built platform with no terminal objective and growing comprehension load remains sustainable for one person. I reason to verdict before stating it, and I deliberately ran a verdict-inverting reading (below) that genuinely tempers the drift critique without erasing it.\",\n  \"verdict\": \"This is sound and impressively disciplined as a working system, but it is drifting from its stated identity into an open-ended, self-built platform with no defined 'done', a heavy and version-stratified comprehension load, and at least one real production-data hygiene leak. Keep it — but set a stopping condition and a consolidation budget before the next version.\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-identity-drift\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The README/CLAUDE.md North Star is 'Anchor - Productivity System for J.C. Liechty', but the observed artifact is overwhelmingly an R&D agent-orchestration platform: 261 api/rnd endpoints vs a handful of task endpoints, the four largest modules are all R&D-surface, and the productivity core (DASHBOARD.md task dates) appears static since ~2026-05-07 while v2..v12 + Gandalf were built. Critically, each version has its OWN planning/rnd-vN/MASTER-PLAN, but there is no single objective statement governing what the R&D surface as a whole is FOR or when it is DONE. Twelve versions in seven weeks with no terminal objective is an open-ended build with no stopping condition. This is the verdict-inverting candidate AND the operator-wrong finding: the operator's evident preference is to keep shipping versions; the finding is that the ABSENCE of a done-definition is itself the top risk, which runs against that preference.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"The artifact no longer matches its stated North Star, and the R&D surface has no overarching objective or definition-of-done; this is the single most consequential issue.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-version-strata\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Every version 'EXTENDS existing seams' rather than consolidating them, so core modules now carry 6-10 layered generations of concern: terminal_session.py 3,170 LOC, effort_history.py 3,115, summarizer.py 1,894, and anchor_gui.py a 15,302-LOC single file mixing HTML/CSS/JS-in-f-strings/HTTP-handlers/change-ops. The 21k-word CLAUDE.md documents each version's seam-deltas in extraordinary prose detail and is effectively the only map of the system. The build is correct and green, but it is increasingly legible only through its own changelog -- a comprehension/maintenance debt that compounds per version.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Accumulating version strata on the same seams/files is a real and compounding comprehension cost, independent of current correctness.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-registry-pollution\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The CLAUDE.md's most-repeated safety invariant is that every test/healthcheck uses temp dirs torn down afterward and 'never touches the real registry/:8777'. Yet the LIVE rnd_registry.json contains ~20 retired temp-folder 'projects' (C:\\\\Users\\\\john\\\\AppData\\\\Local\\\\Temp\\\\tmp...\\\\test) AND >=3 ACTIVE temp leftovers ('S','P','I'), plus 5 duplicate same-folder 'Anchor' entries. This is direct evidence the temp-isolation invariant has been violated historically (manual runs and/or a pre-guard surface wrote the production registry), and the v2 reconcile_folder / v9 ghost-cleanup+dedup machinery built for exactly this is evidently not being run. rnd_jobs/ also holds 2,712 records with no retention policy.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"The production registry is polluted with test scaffolding and duplicates; the invariant that protects it has leaked, and the existing cleanup tools are unused.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-gui-monolith\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The documented 'how to add a feature' path routes nearly all UI/HTTP/change logic through one 15,302-LOC file, with JS/CSS embedded in Python f-strings (the CLAUDE.md flags the recurring pitfall: every literal brace must be doubled). The project ALREADY vendors static assets (xterm, anchor-term, brand), so the templating-in-f-string fragility is avoidable. The Playwright/DOM gate contains it today, but the correctness surface of 15k LOC of brace-escaped template strings is large and fragile.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"anchor_gui.py is a single-file monolith with an avoidable f-string-templating fragility class.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"d-doc-memory-drift\",\n      \"kind\": \"diagnose\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"The injected CLAUDE.md/persistent memory states v12 'Efforts' is 'NOT merged/deployed -- awaiting John's whole-branch sign-off', but git HEAD on master shows '7c2f51f Merge v12 Efforts to master' and 'bd153e7 Merge Gandalf integration v1', i.e. both are merged and deployed. The system's own durable memory lags the repo. Low stakes, but this is precisely the claimed-vs-actual drift class Gandalf exists to surface.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Persistent project memory/docs trail ground truth (v12 + Gandalf are merged, memory says otherwise).\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a-comprehension-wall\",\n      \"kind\": \"anticipate\",\n      \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"future_state_condition\": \"It is ~6 months on; a new capability or an external API change (Claude CLI / ConPTY / gh) forces a cross-cutting change, and no single person -- including John -- can hold all 12 version strata + the 15k-LOC anchor_gui.py in head well enough to change it safely; velocity collapses and each change risks a regression the 13-surface healthcheck does not cover.\",\n      \"enabling_assumption\": \"Development keeps layering new versions onto the same seams/files without a consolidation or retirement pass, and the CLAUDE.md changelog remains the primary map of the system.\",\n      \"subject_cardinality\": 1,\n      \"reasoning\": \"A bounded premortem on the sound-but-stratified artifact: the green healthcheck guards behavior per-version but does not reduce the cognitive surface; comprehension cost is the variable that silently crosses a threshold.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"The most likely future wall is comprehension, not correctness -- changes become unsafe-to-make before they become wrong.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a-registry-misact\",\n      \"kind\": \"anticipate\",\n      \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n      \"severity\": \"major\",\n      \"future_state_condition\": \"It is N months on; the production registry (and unbounded rnd_jobs/, already 2,712) has accumulated enough stale/duplicate/temp entries that a real external project (aurora, MBA Teaching AI, Transformer Math, Skill Foundry) is mis-acted-on -- mis-moved on disk, mis-summarized, or pushed to the wrong remote -- because the dashboard resolved a stale or duplicate record.\",\n      \"enabling_assumption\": \"No registry GC/dedup runs automatically, the temp-pollution leak is not closed at its source, and rnd_jobs/ gets no retention policy.\",\n      \"subject_cardinality\": 1,\n      \"reasoning\": \"The guarded on-disk move (v9) and auto-push (v8) are genuinely destructive/outward-facing operations keyed off registry records; a polluted registry turns a data-hygiene smell into an action-on-the-wrong-target hazard.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Registry pollution is currently cosmetic but sits one feature-interaction away from acting on the wrong real project.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"a-gandalf-never-worked-live\",\n      \"kind\": \"anticipate\",\n      \"rung\": \"CLAIMED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"future_state_condition\": \"It is N months on; Gandalf's first-scan auto-run fires an unbounded agentic claude -p run on each newly-registered project, but because the real-claude live-smoke is only a manual deploy-checklist item (explicitly NOT a pytest gate), real runs silently time out / emit unparseable schema / cost more than expected, and honest 'error run' rows accumulate while no one notices Gandalf never actually produced a real read in production.\",\n      \"enabling_assumption\": \"_PROACTIVE_SUMMARY_ENABLED is turned on in prod without the one-time real-claude live-smoke being performed, and the deterministic stub-only healthcheck is mistaken for proof the live path works.\",\n      \"subject_cardinality\": 1,\n      \"reasoning\": \"Everything Gandalf is verified against is stubbed (stub_gandalf_draft / stub_gandalf_host); the live two-stage chain (real claude -> real node host) has, by the project's own deploy note, never been gated -- a classic 'green in CI, untested in prod' seam.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Gandalf's live path is unproven by construction; the risk is silent prod no-op, not a crash.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"s-tooling-eats-mission\",\n      \"kind\": \"situate\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"severity\": \"minor\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"S0 abstraction (domain-neutral): 'a self-maintained system whose tooling layer grows until it absorbs and outpaces the original payload, with no terminal objective governing the tooling layer.' SITUATE fires (central load-bearing claim = a single operator can sustainably run an ever-extending self-built platform; a plausible better-in-class frame exists; stakes >= medium), but per protocol I do NOT self-verify: the relevant best-in-class frames -- internal-platform/framework accretion, the second-system effect, product-vs-platform boundary discipline, explicit definition-of-done / sunset criteria, and complexity-science views of unbounded accretion -- are a needs_verification handoff to researchPrime (no researchPrime ran on this single-family Tier-1 pass). The candidate structure-map (>=2 relational correspondences, asserted, UNVERIFIED): (1) the per-version 'EXTENDS existing seams with no retirement' maps to framework strata that are never deprecated; (2) 'green healthcheck per version but rising changelog-dependence' maps to test-coverage masking architectural entropy. Stated honestly as a frame to investigate, not a verified prescription.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"SITUATE handoff: the 'tooling-eats-the-mission / no-sunset-criteria' pattern is well-studied in engineering and complexity literature; commission researchPrime to verify the best-in-class framing before relying on it. UNVERIFIED here.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nitpicks\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n-mojibake\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"health_reports/2026-06-23.md renders em-dashes/checkmarks as mojibake (e.g. 'Anchor Health Report â€”', 'âœ“') despite the just-committed aa19ab1 'capture stdout as UTF-8 (fix Windows mojibake)'. The encoding fix evidently did not cover the health-report writer's output path.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Windows encoding fragility persists in the health-report writer; low stakes but recurring.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"n-rnd-jobs-unbounded\",\n      \"rung\": \"OBSERVED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"rnd_jobs/ holds 2,712 job records. The 2026-06-16 perf fix made the dashboard hot path O(1) via targeted load_record, but the directory itself has no retention/rotation -- it only ever grows.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"rnd_jobs/ growth is now off the hot path but still unbounded on disk.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"elevations\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-define-done\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"high\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Write ONE North Star + explicit definition-of-done / sunset criteria for the R&D control surface as a whole (not per-version), and adopt a consolidation budget: for the next N versions, every new version must retire or merge at least one prior stratum. This directly attacks d-identity-drift and a-comprehension-wall by replacing 'keep adding versions' with a measurable stopping/consolidation condition.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Set a terminal objective and a 'retire one stratum per new version' budget before v13.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If John's actual goal is open-ended R&D as a craft/practice -- the building IS the point, not a shippable end-state -- then a definition-of-done is a category error that imposes false closure on a deliberately unbounded project, and the right move is to drop the productivity-system framing instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-clean-registry\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"high\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Run the EXISTING v2 reconcile_folder + v9 ghost/cleanup machinery against the live registry now to drop the ~20 temp scaffolds and 5 duplicate Anchor entries; close the temp-pollution leak at its source (prove no surface walk can write the real registry, e.g. assert ANCHOR_DATA_DIR isolation in the offending path); and add a retention/rotation policy to rnd_jobs/. Addresses d-registry-pollution and a-registry-misact using tools already built.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Use the cleanup tools you already shipped, then seal the leak and bound rnd_jobs/.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If the temp/duplicate entries are provably inert everywhere (filtered out of all renders and all destructive ops the way __healthcheck__ is), and the move/push paths re-validate folder_path against disk before acting, then the pollution is cosmetic and the cleanup is unjustified churn.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-gandalf-livesmoke-gate\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Before depending on Gandalf in prod, perform the one-time real claude -p live-smoke from the deploy checklist and keep the first-scan auto-run OFF (or gated behind that smoke passing) until the live two-stage chain is proven to emit parseable schema within the 600s timeout. Addresses a-gandalf-never-worked-live without weakening the stubbed CI gate.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Prove the Gandalf live path once with real claude before enabling auto-run.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If _PROACTIVE_SUMMARY_ENABLED stays off in prod so no auto-run ever fires and Gandalf is only invoked manually (where an honest error row is immediately visible), the existing manual smoke is sufficient and a gate adds nothing.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"e-extract-gui-assets\",\n      \"value_if_true\": \"medium\",\n      \"rung\": \"UNVERIFIED\",\n      \"reasoning\": \"Extract the anchor_gui.py JS/CSS out of Python f-strings into static vendored assets (you already serve vendor/xterm, vendor/anchor-term, vendor/brand via traversal-safe routes), eliminating the brace-doubling fragility class and shrinking the 15.3k-LOC monolith. Addresses d-gui-monolith.\",\n      \"verdict\": \"Move embedded JS/CSS to vendored static files to kill the f-string brace hazard and shrink the monolith.\",\n      \"what_would_refute_it\": \"If f-string templating has caused zero shipped UI defects across v2..v12 (the brace-doubling discipline + Playwright gate fully contain it), the extraction is churn against a non-problem and risks introducing the very regressions it aims to prevent.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"8879e2bf-702b-4c2f-a33b-7fb98e48e304","total_cost_usd":2.4033379999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":6948,"cache_creation_input_tokens":115044,"cache_read_input_tokens":1388266,"output_tokens":20788,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":115044,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12730,"cache_read_input_tokens":133813,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2092,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2092},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":4235,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.004325,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-8[1m]":{"inputTokens":6948,"outputTokens":20788,"cacheReadInputTokens":1388266,"cacheCreationInputTokens":115044,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.399013,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[{"tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01SVR7FzyouLsmME6z1P3YAX","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\runtime\\RAW-DRAFT-CONTRACT.md"}},{"tool_name":"Read","tool_use_id":"toolu_01CJbugGXeuRMzcLg6oZAFqQ","tool_input":{"file_path":"C:\\dev\\Skill Foundry\\skills\\gandalf\\schema\\advisor-output.schema.json"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01KEPkTGrsJu12AU4Srvf3Ha","tool_input":{"command":"echo \"=== Python module count + total LOC ===\" && find . -maxdepth 1 -name \"*.py\" | wc -l && find . -maxde